# A bug of the prototype (tester report 30.10.2026, EU discs, with pictures): the Mercenaries' time pick-ups showed
# "50PTASsec. extended!" and "Bonus Time! You have 900PTASsec. ...". The pick-up message of the money-type items
# (sce_at.cpp, two copies) sets the number with attribute 0x10000000, which appends the PTAS glyph after the digits
# (Message::code0a) - right for pesetas (message 0x14), wrong for the added time (item 0x73, message 0x94) and the
# bonus time (item 0x75, message 0x95). The bonus time also showed m_bonus_point, the frames given to
# MercSysSetBonusTime (30 s * 30 = 900); m_bonus_point only feeds this message and now holds the seconds. The time
# given to the game is unchanged. Not changed: the pick-up sound (SndCall(0, 0x10), the money's; the tester thinks
# the healing items' sound is right) until the European code is read. All discs.
--- a/src/game/item.cpp
+++ b/src/game/item.cpp
@@ -1887,7 +1887,7 @@
         if (num == 0) {
             num = 30;
         }
-        m_bonus_point = num * 30;
+        m_bonus_point = num; /* port (patch 0161): the seconds the message shows, not frames */
         MercSysSetBonusTime(num * 30);
         return 1;
     }
--- a/src/game/sce_at.cpp
